\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The axis that separates the survivors.} (a)~Worst-case per-patient score shift under camera rotation (log scale): the certified models (EGRU, EGNN) hold a patient's score to $\sim \!10^{-5}$~MAD, six orders of magnitude below the augmented and unaugmented transformers. InvariantGRU is exactly $0$ and Canon-PCA empirically $\approx 0$, but unbounded off distribution. (b)~Why the cheap canonicalization alternative is not a guarantee: its PCA frame flips by $>45^\circ $ on $21\%$ of frame transitions and sits within an eigen-gap of $0.05$ of degeneracy on $18\%$ of frames.}}{6}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
